note[grice/unavailable-import]: Can't use the types of an imported module

The module `dependent`, at `src/dependent.gleam`, reaches the module
`dep/inner` through the modules it imports, and girard, the type inference
grice uses, couldn't use it. It's a dependency module, which glance can't
parse: it stopped at line 2, column 1 of its source. Types that depend on
it may be incomplete, so typed rules get no answers in this module.

Hint: If the package builds, glance doesn't support its syntax yet, so
please report it to glance.

note[grice/uninferred-module]: Can't infer the types of a module

girard, the type inference grice uses, returned no types for the module
`lonely`, at `src/lonely.gleam`. Rules still ran on it, but typed rules got
no answers about it, so they may have missed problems there.

Hint: If `gleam build` accepts this code, it's a gap in girard, the type
inference grice uses, so please report it at
https://github.com/alvivi/girard/issues.

note[grice/missing-package]: A dependency's sources are missing

The package `hexdep` is in `manifest.toml`, but `build/packages/hexdep/src`
isn't a directory, so girard, the type inference grice uses, can't read its
modules. Types that come from them may be incomplete.

Hint: Run `gleam deps download`.

note[grice/incomplete-project]: Can't see the whole project

The rule `fixture/whole-project-view` sees every module of the project, but
grice couldn't read all of it, so it didn't run: `src/broken.gleam` doesn't
parse and `test/app_test.gleam` couldn't be read (No such file). A claim
about the whole project can't rest on part of it.

Hint: If `gleam build` accepts a module that doesn't parse, glance, which
grice reads Gleam code with, doesn't support its syntax yet, so please
report it to glance. Check that each file that couldn't be read is there
and that you can read it; a Gleam module must also be UTF-8.

warning[fixture/no-echo]: Echo left in the code
  ┌─ src/app.gleam:4:3
  │
4 │   echo 2
  │   ^^^^^^ This prints when it runs

`echo` prints its value each time it runs.

Hint: Remove it once you're done debugging.

warning[grice/unused-suppression]: Unused suppression
  ┌─ src/app.gleam:7:1
  │
7 │ // grice-ignore fixture/no-echo: Nothing here prints.
  │ ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ This hides nothing

This suppression hides nothing: no diagnostic of the rule `fixture/no-echo`
is left to hide on line 8, the next line of code.

Hint: Fix the suppression, or remove it. Write `// grice-ignore <rule
code>: <reason>` on its own line, above the code it covers, or `//
grice-ignore-file <rule code>: <reason>` before the module's first line of
code to cover the whole module.

warning[grice/invalid-suppression]: Invalid suppression
   ┌─ src/app.gleam:12:1
   │
12 │ // grice-ignore fixture/no-echo
   │ ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ This gives no reason

A suppression says why the rule doesn't apply, after a colon that follows
the rule code, but this one gives no reason. It hides nothing.

Hint: Write `// grice-ignore <rule code>: <reason>` on its own line, above
the code it covers, or `// grice-ignore-file <rule code>: <reason>` before
the module's first line of code to cover the whole module.

note[grice/untyped-definition]: Can't infer the types of this definition
   ┌─ src/app.gleam:13:1
   │
13 │ pub fn skipped() {
   │ ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ girard couldn't type this definition

girard couldn't type `skipped`: type mismatch: Int vs String. Typed rules
get no answers about the code inside it, so they may miss problems there.

Hint: If `gleam build` accepts this code, it's a gap in girard, the type
inference grice uses, so please report it at
https://github.com/alvivi/girard/issues.

error[grice/parse-error]: Can't parse this module
  ┌─ src/broken.gleam:1:1
  │
1 │ pub fn (
  │ ^^^ glance didn't expect this

grice reads Gleam code with glance, and glance couldn't parse this file. No
rule ran on it, and the modules that import it may lose type information.

Hint: If `gleam build` accepts this file, glance doesn't support its syntax
yet, so please report it to glance.

note[grice/unavailable-import]: Can't use the types of an imported module
  ┌─ src/nameless.gleam:1:1
  │
1 │ import nowhere
  │ ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ girard couldn't use this

girard, the type inference grice uses, couldn't use the module `nowhere`,
which this module imports. No module of the project or of its dependencies
has that name. Types that depend on it may be incomplete, so typed rules
get no answers in this module.

Hint: Check the import. If the module belongs to a dependency, `gleam deps
download` fetches its sources.

1 error, 3 warnings and 6 notes in 5 modules, 1 hidden by ignores and
suppressions.
Coverage is incomplete: 1 module doesn't parse, 1 definition in 1 module
